# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: UnionKingdom | Scene: UnionKingdom4

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah stood out on the balcony of her room, overlooking her city. Her kingdom."
    new "Sarah se paró en el balcón de su habitación, mirando a su ciudad. Su reino."

    old "Out below, the many lights, creeping out from houses and businesses, cut through the otherwise dark night."
    new "Abajo, la multitud de luces que surgían de las casas y los negocios cortaba el cielo nocturno, que de otro modo estaba oscuro."

    old "Even beyond the walls of the city, she could spot the occasional light. It had not always been like that."
    new "Incluso más allá de los muros de la ciudad, podía distinguir las ocasionales luces. No siempre había sido así."

    old "So much life."
    new "Tanta vida."

    old "Her people thrived. What more could have ever asked for."
    new "Su gente prosperaba. ¿Qué más podrían haber deseado?"

    old "What do you say, Father?"
    new "¿Qué dices, padre?"

    old "Her voice carried out into the lonely night."
    new "Su voz se extendió hacia la noche solitaria."

    old "Am I all that you had hoped me to be?"
    new "¿Soy todo lo que esperabas de mí?"

    old "Only the wind answered her."
    new "Solo el viento respondió a ella."

    old "As always, she would be left to ponder those questions herself."
    new "Como siempre, se quedaría a reflexionar sobre esas preguntas por su cuenta."

    old "Who were you talking to?"
    new "¿A quién estabas hablando?"

    old "Sarah spun around, surprised at Varga's sudden appearance."
    new "Sarah giró en redondo, sorprendida por la aparición repentina de Varga."

    old "Her husband, loyal and unwavering. A rock. His plain smile which had no hidden nature."
    new "Su esposo, leal e inquebrantable. Una roca. Su sonrisa franca que no ocultaba nada."

    old "Her Warmaster, loyal and unwavering. One of the few people that she dared to trust blindly."
    new "Su Gran Maestra, leal e inquebrantable. Uno de los pocos a quienes se atrevía a confiar ciegamente."

    old "I was just...thinking out loud."
    new "Solo estaba... pensando en voz alta."

    old "She saw him shrug."
    new "La vio encoger los hombros."

    old "It's fine if you don't want to tell me."
    new "No importa si no quieres decírmelo."

    old "I sometimes talk to the wind too."
    new "A veces también hablo con el viento."

    old "Really, whispering secrets?"
    new "¿De verdad, susurrando secretos?"

    old "Varga walked forward and leaned on the edge of the balcony, looking out over the capital."
    new "Varga avanzó y se apoyó en el borde de la balconada, mirando hacia la capital."

    old "We all have parts to ourself that we fear to show to others."
    new "Todos tenemos partes de nosotros mismos que tememos mostrar a los demás."

    old "Sarah looked at him. Tall and strong, she wondered if her really feared anything."
    new "Sarah lo miró. Alto y fuerte, se preguntó si realmente temía algo."

    old "And what fears do you have then?"
    new "¿Y qué temores tienes entonces?"

    old "I thought we were keeping our secrets to ourself."
    new "Creí que estábamos guardando nuestros secretos entre nosotros."

    old "Tell Varga what you were saying"
    new "Cuéntale a Varga lo que estabas diciendo"

    old "Sarah let her smile slip."
    new "Sarah dejó que su sonrisa se desvaneciera."

    old "I was talking to my father."
    new "Estaba hablando con mi padre."

    old "She saw his face frown."
    new "Vió cómo su frente se fruncía."

    old "Your father?"
    new "¿Tu padre?"

    old "Sometimes when I'm alone I like to ask him questions out loud."
    new "A veces, cuando estoy sola, me gusta hacerle preguntas en voz alta."

    old "I know there won't be any answers but it feels like...I imagine he can hear me."
    new "Sé que no habrá respuestas, pero siento que... imagino que puede oírme."

    old "If that makes me sound crazy-"
    new "Si eso me hace sonar loca,"

    old "Not at all."
    new "Para nada."

    old "He paused for a brief moment, then continued with a hesitant tremor in his voice."
    new "Pausó por un breve instante y luego continuó con una voz vacilante."

    old "Would you mind if I asked you what you talk to him about?"
    new "¿Te importaría que te preguntara con qué le hablas?"

    old "Sarah felt tears stinging in her face."
    new "Sarah sintió que las lágrimas le ardían en la cara."

    old "He died before he ever saw what became of me and Thomas...before we were ever really tested."
    new "Murió antes de ver lo que me pasó a mí y a Thomas...antes de que realmente nos probáramos."

    old "I just...I wish I could know if he's proud of me or not."
    new "Solo... solo quisiera saber si se siente orgulloso de mí o no."

    old "If he looks at me and is pleased or if he's dissapointed."
    new "Si me mira y queda satisfecho o si se decepciona."

    old "Varga reached over, placing his hand over hers."
    new "Varga se inclinó y colocó su mano sobre la de ella."

    old "How could he ever be anything other than proud? Look at all you have done."
    new "¿Cómo podría ser algo distinto que orgulloso? Mira todo lo que has logrado."

    old "Sarah laughed as she looked at him."
    new "Sarah rió al mirarlo."

    old "You never knew my father, not really. He could be very strict. Very demanding."
    new "Nunca supiste de mi padre, no realmente. Podía ser muy estricto. Muy exigente."

    old "She paused and looked back out over the city."
    new "Pausó y miró de nuevo hacia la ciudad."

    old "But he could just as easily be so loving and caring..."
    new "Pero también podría ser tan cariñoso y atento..."

    old "I just...I had so many years with him, more than I had with my mother, but some days I still wonder how much I ever knew him."
    new "Solo... pasé tantos años con él, más de los que pasé con mi madre, pero algunos días aún me pregunto cuánto lo conocí realmente."

    old "He was always partly my father, and partly the king."
    new "Siempre fue en parte mi padre y en parte el rey."

    old "Sarah saw Varga look at her. He didn't speak, but his eyes said plenty."
    new "Sarah vio que Varga la miraba. No habló, pero sus ojos decían mucho."

    old "She turned to him."
    new "Se volvió hacia él."

    old "Now you."
    new "Ahora tú."

    old "Me?"
    new "¿Yo?"

    old "He seemed startled."
    new "Parecía sobresaltado."

    old "I gave you my secret, what about you? What do you whisper about when nobody is listening?"
    new "Te di mi secreto, ¿y tú? ¿De qué susurras cuando nadie escucha?"

    old "Varga's own smile slowly faded."
    new "La propia sonrisa de Varga se desvaneció lentamente."

    old "I remember what I did, back in my home of Northwood."
    new "Recuerdo lo que hice, en mi hogar de Northwood."

    old "The peasant uprising that he had helped put down in his own hometown. The act that had won him his title and nobility."
    new "La revuelta campesina que él ayudó a sofocar en su propia ciudad natal. El acto que le valió su título y nobleza."

    old "I run through all the names and faces of those that died. Those that I can remember, at least."
    new "Recorro todos los nombres y rostros de aquellos que murieron. De los que puedo recordar, al menos."

    old "You torture yourself? Why?"
    new "¿Te atormentas a ti misma? ¿Por qué?"

    old "Varga turned away from her, a pained expression on his face."
    new "Varga se volvió de espaldas a ella, con una expresión de dolor en el rostro."

    old "Some wars are pure and clean. My war was not that."
    new "Algunas guerras son puras y limpias. La mía no lo fue."

    old "There were fathers that killed sons and sons that killed fathers. Brother killing brother."
    new "Hubo padres que mataron a hijos e hijos que mataron a padres. Hermanos matando hermanos."

    old "Some of the men that rose up...their reasons were not without merit."
    new "Algunos de los hombres que se levantaron... sus razones no carecían de mérito."

    old "Sarah watched as his face sank into a memory."
    new "Sarah observó cómo su rostro se sumergía en un recuerdo."

    old "There were those I killed that deserved everything they got and more."
    new "Había quienes maté y que merecían todo lo que recibieron, y mucho más."

    old "Bandits and rapists that took pleasure in the chaos."
    new "Bandidos y violadores que disfrutaban del caos."

    old "But in the end, there were also those who rebelled because their farms had failed and their children were hungry."
    new "Pero al final, también hubo quienes se rebelaron porque sus granjas habían fallado y sus hijos tenían hambre."

    old "I killed them all the same."
    new "Los maté a todos de la misma manera."

    old "Sarah could see it pained him to even speak of it."
    new "Sarah podía ver que le dolía incluso mencionarlo."

    old "You did it for the country...to keep it together."
    new "Lo hiciste por el país... para mantenerlo unido."

    old "I did."
    new "Yo lo hice."

    old "And I don't regret doing it."
    new "Y no me arrepiento de haberlo hecho."

    old "But...sometimes the things we do, even if we don't regret them...they still seem to cling to us."
    new "Pero... a veces las cosas que hacemos, incluso si no nos arrepentimos... parecen seguirnos."

    old "Sarah reached over and touched his arm."
    new "Sarah se inclinó y tocó su brazo."

    old "I think you are a good person, Varga."
    new "Creo que eres una buena persona, Varga."

    old "Varga smiled as he turned to her."
    new "Varga sonrió al girarse hacia ella."

    old "And I think the same of you, Sarah."
    new "Y creo que lo mismo pienso de ti, Sarah."

    old "But does either of us heal quite so easily?"
    new "¿Pero acaso alguno de nosotros sana tan fácilmente?"

    old "Sarah smiled at his words, knowing they were true."
    new "Sarah sonrió a sus palabras, sabiendo que eran ciertas."

    old "Don't tell him what you were saying"
    new "No le digas lo que estabas diciendo"

    old "Fine, to each our own secrets then."
    new "Bien, cada uno sus propios secretos entonces."

    old "For a while, the two leaned across the balcony in silence."
    new "Por un tiempo, los dos se apoyaron en el balcón en silencio."

    old "You are going to Normandi soon..."
    new "Pronto irás a Normandía..."

    old "Have you given any consideration as to who will go with you?"
    new "¿Has pensado en quién te acompañará?"

    old "Sarah smiled. She knew what he would offer before he even said it."
    new "Sarah sonrió. Sabía qué ofrecería antes de que siquiera lo dijera."

    old "I suspect you wish to ask me something..."
    new "Sospecho que deseas preguntarme algo..."

    old "Varga turned to her."
    new "Varga se volvió hacia ella."

    old "Allow me to go with you."
    new "Permíteme ir contigo."

    old "As your husband, I can keep you safe."
    new "Como tu esposo, puedo mantenerte a salvo."

    old "As your Warmaster, I can keep you safe."
    new "Como tu Warmaster, puedo mantenerte a salvo."

    old "I will have a small army to keep me safe."
    new "Tendré un pequeño ejército para mantenerme a salvo."

    old "And should she truly want to hurt me, I will be in the heart of her nation. Her castle."
    new "Y si ella realmente quisiera lastimarme, estaré en el corazón de su nación. En su castillo."

    old "Still, to have me would-"
    new "Aún así, tenerme a mí -"

    old "Would do what?"
    new "¿Qué haría?"

    old "She saw the pain on his face."
    new "Vio el dolor en su rostro."

    old "I do not mean to insult you, Varga."
    new "No pretendo insultarte, Varga."

    old "There are few in this world that I would put above you in military skill, or even simply as a warrior in your own right."
    new "Hay pocos en este mundo que pondría por encima de ti en habilidad militar, o incluso simplemente como guerrera en tu propio derecho."

    old "But what of it?"
    new "¿Y qué más?"

    old "If all this turns out to be a trap, your presence would change nothing."
    new "Si todo esto resulta ser una trampa, tu presencia no cambiaría nada."

    old "And if I knew in my final moments that I had lured you along with me to a pointless death..."
    new "Y si supiera en mis últimos momentos que te he arrastrado conmigo hacia una muerte inútil..."

    old "And what of our children?"
    new "¿Y qué pasará con nuestros hijos?"

    old "She saw a moment of realization dawn on his face."
    new "Vio un momento de comprensión iluminarse en su rostro."

    old "I..."
    new "..."

    old "We would orphan them...I could never live with myself."
    new "Nos quedaríamos huérfanos... nunca podría vivir conmigo misma."

    old "No...though I wish I could have you by my side, I must go and do this myself."
    new "No... aunque deseara tenerla a mi lado, debo ir y hacerlo por mí misma."

    old "She smiled as she met his eyes. Dark brown, the light dancing in them."
    new "Sonrió al encontrarse con sus ojos. Marrón oscuro, la luz bailando en ellos."

    old "Besides, if she betrays me, you will have a great task to perform."
    new "Además, si me traiciona, tendrás una gran tarea por delante."

    old "Task?"
    new "¿Tarea?"

    old "To avenge me. To bring my army and tear down every brick and stone of her country."
    new "Para vengarme. Para traer mi ejército y derribar cada ladrillo y piedra de su país."

    old "You make sport of it. Do you not fear death? Imprisonment?"
    new "Te burlas de ello. ¿No temes la muerte? ¿La prisión?"

    old "I fear it only in healthy amounts. Fear it too much, and the fear becomes worse than the fate."
    new "Temo que solo en cantidades saludables. Temerlo demasiado, y el temor se vuelve peor que el destino."

    old "Varag shook his head."
    new "Varag sacudió la cabeza."

    old "You're something else, Sarah."
    new "Eres otra cosa, Sarah."

    old "Sarah laughed and seized her husband's arm."
    new "Sarah rió y se aferró al brazo de su esposo."

    old "Perhaps I am mad, but you and I are made for each other, so what does that say of you?"
    new "Quizás estoy loca, pero tú y yo estamos hechos el uno para el otro; ¿qué dice eso de ti?"

    old "Either that I am mad as well, or perhaps so blinded by love that I can see no flaws in you."
    new "O es que también estoy loco, o quizás estoy tan ciego por el amor que no veo ningún defecto en ti."

    old "Sarah smiled and threw her arms around her husband's neck."
    new "Sarah sonrió y se lanzó a abrazar el cuello de su esposo."

    old "She pulled herself up to match his height and kissed him deeply."
    new "Se levantó hasta igualar su altura y lo besó profundamente."

    old "I will leave soon, and I will not be back for many weeks."
    new "Me iré pronto y no volveré por muchas semanas."

    old "Her husband smiled, her intentions clear."
    new "Su marido sonrió, sus intenciones claras."

    old "Better we not waste what little time we have then."
    new "Más vale que no desperdicemos el poco tiempo que nos queda."

    old "Waste?"
    new "¿Desperdicio?"

    old "Sarah dragged him into their room and pulled him onto their bed."
    new "Sarah lo arrastró a su habitación y lo tiró sobre la cama."

    old "I shall soon be gone for weeks, best you make sure I don't forget you."
    new "Pronto estaré ausente durante semanas; mejor asegúrate de que no te olvide."

    old "Varga smiled as he threw away his clothes, revealing his scarred chest."
    new "Varga sonrió mientras se quitaba la ropa, mostrando su pecho cicatrizado."

    old "Trust me."
    new "Confía en mí."

    old "You won't soon forget tonight."
    new "No olvidarás esta noche pronto."

    old "And as he seized on her and ripped away her clothes, Sarah found herself quickly lost to her husband's hands."
    new "Y al apoderarse de ella y arrancarle la ropa, Sarah se encontró rápidamente perdida en las manos de su esposo."

    old "His fingers deftly moving across her body, playing every part of her as only he could."
    new "Sus dedos se movían con destreza por su cuerpo, tocando cada parte de ella como solo él podía."

    old "Though she had always come to know him as a skilled lover, something else possessed him that night."
    new "Aunque siempre lo había conocido como un amante hábil, algo más lo poseía esa noche."

    old "She cried out to the movement of his fingers."
    new "Ella gritó ante el movimiento de sus dedos."

    old "Came to the touch of his tongue."
    new "Tocó con la lengua."

    old "Moaned his name as he bend her over and took her."
    new "Gimió su nombre mientras lo doblaba sobre ella y se la follaba."

    old "Whispered his name in worship as she rode on top of him."
    new "Susurró su nombre en adoración mientras ella lo montaba."

    old "All the time, he never tired and all the time she could see his eyes filled with his desire for her."
    new "Todo el tiempo, él nunca se cansaba y todo el tiempo ella podía ver sus ojos llenos de deseo por ella."

    old "His broad and powerful hands cupped her breasts, grazing her nipples."
    new "Sus manos anchas y poderosas rodearon sus pechos, rozando sus mamilas."

    old "The marathon of sex had ruined her body and left her vulnerable to even the slightest of touch."
    new "El maratón de sexo había arruinado su cuerpo y la había dejado vulnerable incluso al más mínimo contacto."

    old "Pleasure so fully drowned out every sinew in her body and every fragment of her mind that she could no longer even conceive of holding back."
    new "El placer inundó tan completamente cada fibra de su cuerpo y cada fragmento de su mente que ya no podía ni siquiera concebir la posibilidad de contenerse."

    old "When she came, again and again, she cried out his name, losing even the pretense of virtue."
    new "Cuando llegó, una y otra vez, gritó su nombre, perdiendo incluso la pretensión de virtud."

    old "She loved him fully. Yes with her heart, but she loved him also in this moment for the raw physicality of him."
    new "Lo amaba por completo. Sí, con todo su corazón, pero también lo amaba en este momento por la crudeza física de él."

    old "For his body and every part of it."
    new "Por su cuerpo y por cada una de sus partes."

    old "There were moments were she longed to be loved by him, held by him, and to hear him whisper sweet words."
    new "Hubo momentos en los que anhelaba ser amada por él, sostenida por él, y escucharle susurrar palabras dulces."

    old "And then there were nights like this, were she longed for him to destroy every part of her."
    new "Y luego llegaban las noches como esta, en las que ansiaba que él destruyera cada parte de ella."

    old "To wreck every limb in her body with pleasure."
    new "Destrozar cada parte de su cuerpo con placer."

    old "Times to be wanted as a wife. Times to be wanted as a woman."
    new "Tiempo de ser deseada como esposa. Tiempo de ser deseada como mujer."

    old "Looking down on top of him, riding him with what little strength she had left, she could see that in him, she found all of it."
    new "Mirando hacia abajo sobre él, montándolo con la poca fuerza que le quedaba, podía ver que en él encontraba todo."

    old "The love of a husband and the desire of a man."
    new "El amor de un esposo y el deseo de un hombre."

    old "And though the stories of old had told her that these things existed in contrast to one another, she now saw they instead both existed in him."
    new "Aunque las historias antiguas le habían dicho que estas cosas existían en contraste entre sí, ahora veía que ambas coexistían en él."

    old "He was a husband who loved her, as well as a man who desired her for her body."
    new "Era un esposo que la amaba, así como un hombre que deseaba su cuerpo."

    old "And rather than one contrasting with the other, they rather appeared to instead each heighten the other."
    new "Y en lugar de contrastar la una con la otra, parecían por el contrario realzar mutuamente."

    old "For his love he was a better man, and for his desire a better husband."
    new "Por su amor era un hombre mejor, y por su deseo, un marido mejor."

    old "So singular a person. And he belonged to her and her alone, just as she did to him."
    new "¡Qué tan singular! Él pertenecía a ella y solo a ella, al igual que ella le pertenecía a él."

    old "I love you."
    new "Te amo."

    old "She spoke the words through heavy breaths."
    new "Ella pronunció las palabras entre pesadas respiraciones."

    old "She felt his powerful hands tighten around her waist, guiding her back and forth as she rode him, controlling the tempo."
    new "Sintió cómo sus poderosas manos se aferraban a su cintura, guiándola de adelante hacia atrás mientras ella lo montaba, controlando el ritmo."

    old "I love you too..."
    new "Yo también te quiero..."

    old "His words were equally strained from the exhaustion."
    new "Sus palabras también estaban tensas por el agotamiento."

    old "Sarah cried out as she came once again, partly from his efforts and partly from his words."
    new "Sarah gritó mientras llegaba una vez más, en parte por sus esfuerzos y en parte por sus palabras."

    old "She heard her husband grunting beneath her, his member swelling inside of her."
    new "Escuché a mi esposo gemir bajo mí, sintiendo cómo su polla se hincha dentro de ella."

    old "Sarah could feel him spewing his seed deep into her and she wished for all she could that it would take root."
    new "Sarah podía sentir cómo él expulsaba su semilla profundamente dentro de ella y deseaba con todo su corazón que echara raíces."

    old "Each crying out in peaking pleasure, they finished together."
    new "Cada uno gritando con placer al límite, terminaron juntos."

    old "Her body completely exhausted, she collapsed forward into his embrace."
    new "Agotada y aliviada, se derrumbó hacia adelante en su abrazo."

    old "She felt his broad and powerful arms wrap around her, and there he kept her."
    new "Sintió cómo sus amplios y poderosos brazos la envolvían, y allí la mantuvo."

    old "Each whispered words of love as they slowly drifted into sleep."
    new "Cada uno susurró palabras de amor mientras lentamente se adormecían."

    old "Sarah was walking through the cold and dark hallways of the castle."
    new "Sarah caminaba por los fríos y oscuros pasillos del castillo."

    old "She had made her decisison to attend the Union Council, but there was so much more to do."
    new "Había tomado la decisión de asistir al Consejo de la Unión, pero había mucho más por hacer."

    old "So much more to consider."
    new "Hay tanto más por considerar."

    old "Walking the halls at night had an odd meditative effect on her that she appreciated in times of trouble."
    new "Caminar por los pasillos de noche tenía un extraño efecto meditativo en ella que apreciaba en tiempos de dificultad."

    old "Sarah had made but a few rounds when she suddenly saw a shadow move from the corner of her eyes."
    new "Sarah dio apenas unas vueltas cuando de repente vio cómo una sombra se movía en el rincón de su vista."

    old "You have terrible guards."
    new "Tienes guardias terribles."

    old "Lily!"
    new "¡Lily!"

    old "You scared me to death!"
    new "¡Me asustaste hasta la muerte!"

    old "I thought you weren't going to be back for days!"
    new "Pensé que no volverías por días!"

    old "Well, the whole dispute was nothing that a few threats couldn't solve."
    new "Bueno, toda la disputa era algo que unas pocas amenazas no podían resolver."

    old "Don't tell me you really threatend them?"
    new "¿No me dices que realmente los amenazaste?"

    old "Fine, then I won't tell you."
    new "Bien, entonces no te lo diré."

    old "She laughed at her own joke."
    new "Rió de su propia broma."

    old "It wasn't her place to tell Lily how to run her own noble House, but still she hoped she was partially joking."
    new "No era su lugar decirle a Lily cómo administrar su propia casa noble, pero aún así esperaba que estuviera parcialmente bromeando."

    old "Whatever it took, I'm happy to see you back."
    new "No importa lo que haya costado, estoy feliz de verte de vuelta."

    old "Lily looked at her, suddenly serious."
    new "Lily la miró de pronto con seriedad."

    old "And I was happy to see you, Sarah."
    new "Y me alegré de verte, Sarah."

    old "Even went and bought a gift for you. You know how hard it is to buy something for someone that has everything?"
    new "Incluso fue a comprar un regalo para ti. ¿Sabes lo difícil que es comprarle algo a alguien que ya tiene de todo?"

    old "A gift?"
    new "¿Un regalo?"

    old "Yeah, but that was before I heard the news."
    new "Sí, pero eso fue antes de enterarme de la noticia."

    old "News travelled quickly around Rosanna, even when it was supposed to stay a secret."
    new "Las noticias viajan rápido por Rosanna, incluso cuando se supone que deben permanecer en secreto."

    old "The council..."
    new "El consejo..."

    old "Yeah. Have you lost your mind?"
    new "¿Sí? ¿Te has vuelto loca?"

    old "Lily, I don't-"
    new "Lily, no puedo..."

    old "You have no idea what that bitch Maeiv is up to. She could be luring you into a trap."
    new "No tienes ni idea de lo que esa zorra Maeiv está tramando. Podría estar tentándote a caer en una trampa."

    old "We have considered it, and we thought otherwise."
    new "Lo hemos considerado y llegamos a otra conclusión."

    old "Who thought that?"
    new "¿Quién pensó eso?"

    old "Your pretty-know-nothing counsel members?"
    new "¿Mis bonitas pero tontas consejeras?"

    old "Those highborn idiots couldn't see a trap coming if it was spelled out for them!"
